{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>וַאֲצַוֶּנּוּ</b> (and I will charge him) — and I will rouse him; this is the language of Rashi. But there is no need for this, for the statement of HaShem, <b>חֲזַק וֶאֱמָץ כִּי אַתָּה תָּבִיא</b> (Deuteronomy 31:23) (“Be strong and courageous, for you shall bring”), is itself a commandment, and if he had been sluggish and not done so, he would have been liable to death. And it is possible that the meaning of <b>וַאֲצַוֶּנּוּ</b> is: that I will appoint him as leader and issue commands concerning Israel, as I explained in the verse וְצִוִּיתָה אוֹתוֹ לְעֵינֵיהֶם (Numbers 27:19)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T02:57:14.147305965Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}